{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And his anger burned, etc. And he struck his hands, etc.</b> Meaning: His anger burned, and his rage subsided through the clapping of his hands. The sense is that the clapping cooled and calmed the anger." "<b>You have blessed, blessed.</b> Meaning: You pronounced a blessing that contained no curse within it. The proof is that you said, ״מְבָרְכֶיךָ בָרוּךְ וְאֹרְרֶיךָ אָרוּר״ — and according to what I have written, that Balaam's intention was to cause harm, Balak did not sense this intention."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:13:43.304290276Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}